46:     """Recolor every candidate object whose run-compressed shape matches the single prototype object, allowing rotation and reflection.
47:     Input structure
48:     A black-background grid contains exactly two foreground colors: one color forms a single prototype object, and the other forms multiple candidate objects.
49:     Rule
50:     Crop each object to its bbox, collapse adjacent identical rows and columns to remove stretch, and recolor every candidate whose collapsed mask is a rotation or reflection of the prototype's collapsed mask.
51:     Key insight
52:     The prototype is a line-drawing symbol; candidate symbols can be stretched in row/column runs, so matching must compare the compressed topology rather than raw size.
53:     """
